      faq_q5: "How does CapEx planning impact long-term value?",
      faq_a5: "CapEx (Capital Expenditure) planning helps you <b>forecast major investments</b> over a 5-year horizon, ensuring you:<ul class='list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1'><li>Avoid costly emergency repairs</li><li>Protect the property’s value and yield</li><li>Make strategic upgrades at the right time</li></ul><br>By understanding the lifecycle of roofs, HVAC units, and other critical systems, you can <b>manage your portfolio proactively</b>, not reactively.",
      
      faq_q6: "Do I still need a Greek Civil Engineer or Lawyer?",
      faq_a6: "Yes. Our role is <b>strictly technical and advisory</b>:<ul class='list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1'><li><b>Civil Engineer (Michanikos):</b> Required for urban planning approvals and legality statements</li><li><b>Lawyer:</b> Needed for title verification and contract execution</li></ul><br>Klehomerie looks for <b>'Pathology'</b>. We are your <b>technical eyes on the ground before</b> you engage the heavy legal machinery.<br>We find the problems so the Engineer knows where to look.<br><br>For the exact boundary between our technical role and their legal one, see our <a href='/scope/' class='text-[--accent-color] font-bold hover:underline'>full scope of service</a>.",
      
      faq_q7: "Who is Klehomerie NOT for?",
